WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.830 --> 00:00:05.380
The orange sky at dawn.

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:09.393
Snow dusted peaks.

00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:16.867
This is the kind of beauty many
of us only see on Instagram.

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:21.300
And this Instagrammer delivers

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:23.423
these views to you for a living.

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:28.030
She's a new kind of celebrity

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:32.403
and she makes money by
promoting things to her fans.

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:37.053
It's a lucrative world with
billions of dollars rushing in.

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:44.540
As technology replaces old jobs,

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:46.970
it's also creating new ones.

00:00:46.970 --> 00:00:50.783
I'm Aki Ito and I'm here to
show you the jobs of the future.

00:00:56.780 --> 00:00:59.433
My name is Meghan Young
and I'm an Influencer.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:03.783
Alright, we're heading
out for our river cruise.

00:01:04.970 --> 00:01:07.170
At first glance, Meghan's job

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:09.210
doesn't seem like a job at all.

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:10.563
Check this out, oooh!

00:01:13.072 --> 00:01:14.940
For a living, I go on outdoor adventures,

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:17.000
take photos of it, and then share it

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:19.393
across social media
platforms when I get home.

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:21.880
But unlike you and me,

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:25.520
Meghan gets paid to share
some of these photos.

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:29.500
She has almost 200,000
followers on Instagram

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:31.190
and all kinds of companies pay her

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:33.470
to endorse their products on her feed.

00:01:33.470 --> 00:01:35.470
It can be things like technical gear

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:37.790
from raincoats to pants to boots.

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:41.180
It can be different snacks that
keep me going on the trail.

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:44.220
And also travel
destinations, which are my,

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:45.640
honestly my favorite things to do

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:48.090
'cause it's really fun to
explore new landscapes.

00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:54.309
Meghan's on track to earn between

00:01:54.309 --> 00:01:58.340
$50,000 and $100,000 over the next year.

00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:00.893
About 10% of her feed is sponsored.

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:07.520
For a story post on Instagram,

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:10.650
that usually starts around $200 per day.

00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:13.690
And then for posts to
the social feed channel,

00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:16.943
about $1,500 or more for one post.

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:19.470
Right now, much of that

00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:21.913
income is helping pay for this home.

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:27.203
Hey!
Nice to meet you.

00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:32.000
Meghan moved in last month
with her partner, Matt.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:35.760
He's a biologist and a
regular fixture on her feed.

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:39.363
What's it like to have a mini
celebrity as a girlfriend?

00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:43.910
The fame, I really don't
think about it that much.

00:02:43.910 --> 00:02:46.140
Except for when you get mad
at me for using my phone.

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:47.340
She uses her phone a lot, yeah.

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:48.470
Yeah?
Yeah.

00:02:48.470 --> 00:02:50.140
Replying to her followers -
Figuring out -

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:51.580
Yeah.
Boundaries of like,

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:52.870
oh, this is work time and this isn't

00:02:52.870 --> 00:02:55.250
work time, it's definitely important.

00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:57.410
It's a conversation we have all the time.

00:02:57.410 --> 00:02:59.940
What's your favorite part of her job?

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:03.230
Probably it's when I get
to go on her adventures.

00:03:03.230 --> 00:03:04.490
Yeah.
Yeah.

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:05.980
Is there stuff in the outdoors

00:03:05.980 --> 00:03:07.690
that you've learned from her?

00:03:07.690 --> 00:03:11.170
I have never been a
person to lay out my gear,

00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:12.980
to make sure I have
everything appropriately

00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:15.033
for each trip, I tend to wing it.

00:03:15.990 --> 00:03:18.330
But yeah, preparedness is definitely

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:19.910
rubbing off a little
bit on me, which is nice

00:03:19.910 --> 00:03:21.940
because you do have to really make sure

00:03:21.940 --> 00:03:23.834
that you bring everything that you need.

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:27.780
This guy's gonna come out

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:31.353
and then this tent and then the boots.

00:03:37.170 --> 00:03:39.160
Tomorrow, Meghan's taking me

00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:42.900
on one of her signature
mountaineering adventures.

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:45.000
I have to make sure that
all the gear is clean,

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:47.900
it's repaired, that we're safe,
everything is ready to go.

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:51.270
She's also packing
products from two companies

00:03:51.270 --> 00:03:53.760
she's hoping to promote on the trip:

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:56.620
a beer company that's an existing client

00:03:56.620 --> 00:03:58.570
and an energy bar maker she's pitching

00:03:58.570 --> 00:04:00.463
for a future sponsorship deal.

00:04:01.830 --> 00:04:04.000
We're planning a four and a half mile hike

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:08.400
up the Cascade Mountains,
climbing around 2,500 feet.

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:11.443
We'll be camping overnight
and then hiking down.

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:19.393
The next day, we get an early start.

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:26.750
Good morning, it's 5:06.

00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:30.130
Cloudy start to the day, rain
and breezy conditions expected

00:04:30.130 --> 00:04:33.230
for Western Washington
with highs in the low 50s.

00:04:33.230 --> 00:04:36.213
And expect showers this evening
and likely for tomorrow.

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:53.130
A few years ago, Meghan was in law school,

00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:56.230
studying to become an
attorney, and it was there

00:04:56.230 --> 00:04:59.350
that mountaineering came
in surprisingly handy.

00:04:59.350 --> 00:05:01.500
In order to get through
the stresses of law school,

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:04.440
I started going back
outside with a vengeance.

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:06.820
I would post photos on Instagram about

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:08.908
the trips we'd been on
and places we had been

00:05:08.908 --> 00:05:11.690
and eventually brands began
to take notice of that

00:05:11.690 --> 00:05:13.280
and reach out to ask if I wanted to

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:14.853
collaborate in different ways.

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:18.980
She ended up deciding
against a career in law

00:05:18.980 --> 00:05:21.810
and after holding an
office job for two years,

00:05:21.810 --> 00:05:25.603
she quit in March to focus on
being an Influencer full time.

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:30.260
There've been tough moments along the way.

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:40.140
Sometimes I get pretty nasty
messages or hateful comments,

00:05:40.140 --> 00:05:43.030
telling me how I am
allowed to use my voice

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:45.053
and how I'm allowed to use my platform.

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:49.863
I block them and I don't
have any qualms about that.

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:53.690
I think that doing this
job, people can think of you

00:05:53.690 --> 00:05:57.410
as less of a real person
but I'm a very real person

00:05:57.410 --> 00:05:59.400
with very real feelings and fears,

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:01.453
so it can be a little weird sometimes.

00:06:06.820 --> 00:06:08.110
And then there's the constant

00:06:08.110 --> 00:06:10.350
pressure to make sure people are liking,

00:06:10.350 --> 00:06:12.623
commenting, and following her feed.

00:06:14.730 --> 00:06:17.350
Metrics are incredibly important

00:06:17.350 --> 00:06:19.930
in the world of social media influencing.

00:06:19.930 --> 00:06:24.760
And early on, I became really
obsessive with checking them.

00:06:24.760 --> 00:06:27.910
And honestly, it got the
point of being exhausting.

00:06:27.910 --> 00:06:30.380
These days, I try not to focus on it

00:06:30.380 --> 00:06:32.890
because it will drive you insane.

00:06:32.890 --> 00:06:34.800
And for me to live a healthy,

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:36.633
balanced life, I can't do that.

00:06:41.150 --> 00:06:43.663
But we've left all that behind in Seattle.

00:06:50.113 --> 00:06:52.780
Oh, it's cold.
It's not warm.

00:06:57.320 --> 00:06:58.680
The blue sky's really nice.

00:06:58.680 --> 00:06:59.900
Hopefully it moves this way.

00:06:59.900 --> 00:07:01.800
Yeah, that's the hardest part about

00:07:01.800 --> 00:07:03.970
this time of year in
the Pacific Northwest,

00:07:03.970 --> 00:07:06.320
when the weather won't cooperate.

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:08.495
What'd you get me into?

00:07:08.495 --> 00:07:09.959
It's gonna be great, let's go.

00:07:09.959 --> 00:07:11.126
Let's do it.

00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:22.130
This was supposed to be a mild hike

00:07:23.690 --> 00:07:25.690
and it's a total breeze for Meghan

00:07:28.440 --> 00:07:29.823
but not so much for me.

00:07:30.690 --> 00:07:31.773
This is not easy.

00:07:35.090 --> 00:07:35.930
I always wanna make sure

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:37.810
we're as safe as possible but there are

00:07:37.810 --> 00:07:38.750
always these moments where we're

00:07:38.750 --> 00:07:41.660
on something exposed or
we're climbing something,

00:07:41.660 --> 00:07:42.980
I'm thinking about, what if there's

00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:44.980
a rock fall and we plummet to our death?

00:07:46.930 --> 00:07:48.230
Those fears are very real.

00:07:57.090 --> 00:08:01.323
So warm outside, you guys, ahh it's crazy.

00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:07.183
Finally, four hours behind schedule,

00:08:08.820 --> 00:08:10.423
we arrive at the campsite.

00:08:12.180 --> 00:08:14.660
Are we here?
Yeah, this looks like.

00:08:15.836 --> 00:08:17.586
Yeah, woo, we did it!

00:08:30.073 --> 00:08:31.620
This is like a really fresh

00:08:31.620 --> 00:08:33.183
layer of snow, which is nice.

00:08:34.430 --> 00:08:36.180
With the weather worsening,

00:08:38.230 --> 00:08:41.127
we start boiling snow to
make water for dinner.

00:08:52.560 --> 00:08:55.260
And remember that beer Meghan
was planning to promote?

00:08:56.730 --> 00:09:00.620
It's way too cold for that
and she scraps her plans

00:09:00.620 --> 00:09:02.993
for an evening photo shoot altogether.

00:09:07.690 --> 00:09:11.206
A little past 7 pm, we
retreat into our tents,

00:09:13.180 --> 00:09:14.853
shivering in our sleeping bags.

00:09:30.690 --> 00:09:34.873
But after the coldest night of
my life, we wake up to this.

00:09:36.960 --> 00:09:40.270
It's the window of good
weather Meghan was hoping for

00:09:40.270 --> 00:09:42.920
and she uses it to stage a sponsored photo

00:09:42.920 --> 00:09:44.863
for the energy bars she brought along.

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:47.870
I'm always trying to think about,

00:09:47.870 --> 00:09:50.620
how do I take something
and make it look at home

00:09:50.620 --> 00:09:54.073
or natural or normal in
these wild landscapes?

00:09:55.660 --> 00:09:57.700
I think a lot of people
will be watching this

00:09:57.700 --> 00:10:00.613
and think that this looks miserable,

00:10:02.179 --> 00:10:03.390
why did you do this?

00:10:03.390 --> 00:10:04.760
So why do you do it?

00:10:04.760 --> 00:10:09.033
I am so happy out here,
it's a little ridiculous.

00:10:10.550 --> 00:10:11.930
You wake up with mornings like this

00:10:11.930 --> 00:10:15.120
and you sort of forget the
sweating and the heavy bags

00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:17.053
and sort of live in that moment.

00:10:18.290 --> 00:10:22.760
And these places, they may
not last, like global warming,

00:10:22.760 --> 00:10:26.363
so I feel this sense of wanting
to see things while I can.

00:10:28.020 --> 00:10:29.340
For now you get this.

00:10:29.340 --> 00:10:33.130
Yeah, not so bad.

00:10:33.130 --> 00:10:35.453
It's a pretty good office, I'll take it.

00:10:45.070 --> 00:10:46.760
Meghan's post of the energy bar

00:10:46.760 --> 00:10:50.200
has now been seen by 16,000 people

00:10:50.200 --> 00:10:52.950
and since our trip, she's
signed sponsorship deals

00:10:52.950 --> 00:10:57.460
with three new clients,
making the $1.6 billion market

00:10:57.460 --> 00:11:00.483
for Instagram Influencers
just a little bigger.

00:11:02.390 --> 00:11:05.450
But the world of social media changes fast

00:11:05.450 --> 00:11:07.190
and Meghan knows there
are plenty of things

00:11:07.190 --> 00:11:09.513
that could derail her newfound career.

00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:12.023
What if Instagram goes away?

00:11:13.820 --> 00:11:16.570
At the end of the day, I have bills to pay

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:19.557
and sometimes you're looking
at your calendar going,

00:11:19.557 --> 00:11:21.040
"Do I have any projects coming up?"

00:11:21.040 --> 00:11:23.543
and those moments are really scary.

00:11:25.455 --> 00:11:27.440
But for now, she can't imagine

00:11:27.440 --> 00:11:29.293
living her life any other way.

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:33.413
Sun came out, so beautiful.

00:11:34.750 --> 00:11:36.870
I've had young women reach out to me

00:11:36.870 --> 00:11:39.270
and say that they've found inspiration

00:11:39.270 --> 00:11:41.573
or they've gone on a
hike or climbed a peak.

00:11:43.580 --> 00:11:45.490
That's the upside to social media,

00:11:45.490 --> 00:11:48.320
you have this ability to inspire people

00:11:48.320 --> 00:11:51.063
and to actually touch
their lives, offline.

00:11:53.470 --> 00:11:54.620
And that's pretty cool.

